    "text": "This solution never moves services or creates binaries. It only schedules \"impl\" tasks, so every output it produces is valid by construction.\n\n1. For each feature, I find the distinct binaries that hold its services.\n2. Features are sorted by users divided by total estimated cost, where cost is the sum of (difficulty + binary size) over those binaries. A feature is skipped if any single task would take at least L days.\n3. Tasks are assigned in that feature order. Each task goes to the engineer who is free earliest, with ties broken by lowest engineer index, which matches the statement's same-day ordering rule.\n4. For each task I compute the congestion term C as the number of tasks already running in that binary at the start day.\n5. Because a feature is never scheduled twice in the same binary, the \"same feature, same binary\" restriction cannot be violated. A wrong duration estimate would only affect the score, not validity.\n6. I stop assigning once the earliest free engineer cannot start before day L.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main(){\n    int L,G,S,B,F,N;\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d %d %d %d\",&L,&G,&S,&B,&F,&N);\n    unordered_map<string,int> id;\n    vector<int> bin(S);\n    vector<int> R(B,0);\n    char buf[64];\n    vector<string> sn(S);\n    for(int i=0;i<S;i++){\n        int b;scanf(\"%s %d\",buf,&b);\n        id[buf]=i;bin[i]=b;R[b]++;\n    }\n    vector<string> fname(F);\n    vector<int> D(F),U(F);\n    vector<vector<int>> fb(F);\n    for(int i=0;i<F;i++){\n        int m;scanf(\"%s %d %d %d\",buf,&m,&D[i],&U[i]);\n        fname[i]=buf;\n        for(int k=0;k<m;k++){\n            scanf(\"%s\",buf);\n            fb[i].push_back(bin[id[buf]]);\n        }\n        sort(fb[i].begin(),fb[i].end());\n        fb[i].erase(unique(fb[i].begin(),fb[i].end()),fb[i].end());\n    }\n    vector<double> pri(F,-1);\n    vector<int> ord;\n    for(int i=0;i<F;i++){\n        bool ok=true;\n        double c=0;\n        for(int b:fb[i]){\n            if(D[i]+R[b]>=L)ok=false;\n            c+=D[i]+R[b];\n        }\n        if(!ok)continue;\n        pri[i]=(double)U[i]/c;\n        ord.push_back(i);\n    }\n    sort(ord.begin(),ord.end(),[&](int a,int b){\n        if(pri[a]!=pri[b])return pri[a]>pri[b];\n        return a<b;\n    });\n    typedef pair<int,int> pii;\n    priority_queue<pii,vector<pii>,greater<pii>> pq;\n    for(int g=0;g<G;g++)pq.push({0,g});\n    vector<vector<int>> active(B);\n    vector<vector<string>> tasks(G);\n    bool stop=false;\n    for(int f:ord){\n        if(stop)break;\n        for(int b:fb[f]){\n            pii t=pq.top();\n            if(t.first>=L){stop=true;break;}\n            pq.pop();\n            auto&a=active[b];\n            size_t w=0;\n            for(size_t k=0;k<a.size();k++)if(a[k]>t.first)a[w++]=a[k];\n            a.resize(w);\n            int C=a.size();\n            int dur=D[f]+R[b]+C;\n            int e=t.first+dur;\n            a.push_back(e);\n            tasks[t.second].push_back(\"impl \"+fname[f]+\" \"+to_string(b));\n            pq.push({e,t.second});\n        }\n    }\n    int E=0;\n    for(int g=0;g<G;g++)if(!tasks[g].empty())E++;\n    string out=to_string(E)+\"\\n\";\n    for(int g=0;g<G;g++)if(!tasks[g].empty()){\n        out+=to_string(tasks[g].size())+\"\\n\";\n        for(auto&s:tasks[g])out+=s+\"\\n\";\n    }\n    fputs(out.c_str(),stdout);\n}\n```",
